---
import { Image } from "astro:assets";
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import lutronBadge from "../images/lutron-preferred-pro.png";
import generacBadge from "../images/generac-certified-installer.webp";
import teslaBadge from "../images/tesla-certified-installer.png";
---

<Layout
  title="Partners & Certifications | Matlack Electric"
  description="Matlack Electric is a certified Lutron Caseta, Lutron RadioRA 3, Generac, and Tesla installer. See the brands we use for lighting control, backup power, EV charging, and networking, and why we choose them."
>
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="container">
      <h1>Our Partners &amp; Certifications</h1>
      <p>
        The products we install say as much about our work as the wiring
        behind the walls. Here's what we're certified in, what we choose to
        install, and why.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="container">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <h2>Certified Installers</h2>
      <p>
        These are the manufacturers we hold formal certifications with -
        training that covers design and programming, not just wiring.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card">
        <Image src={lutronBadge} alt="Lutron - Preferred Pro" class="partner-logo" />
        <br>
        <p>
          We're certified in both of Lutron's core platforms, so the system
          fits your renovation instead of the other way around. Caséta's
          retrofit-friendly dimmers and switches suit smaller projects and
          budgets where opening every wall isn't in the plan, while RadioRA
          3 brings full whole-home lighting control to larger renovations
          that call for it. Either way, our certification means it's
          designed and programmed properly, not just wired.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <Image src={teslaBadge} alt="Tesla - Certified Installer" class="partner-logo" />
        <br>
        <p>
          Tesla's EV charging solutions are second-to-none, even for non-Teslas, and that's
          why we're proud to be certified to install their wall connectors for our clients.
          As a Tesla Certified Installer we can source parts directly from Tesla to ensure a
          smooth installation process.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <Image src={generacBadge} alt="Generac - Certified Installer" class="partner-logo" />
        <br>
        <p>
          Generac is the name most homeowners already know for standby
          generators, and for good reason. As a certified installer, we
          handle sizing, transfer switch installation, and setup to
          Generac's standards - which also keeps your warranty intact.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="container">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <h2>Brands We're Proud to Install</h2>
      <p>
        Beyond our formal certifications, these are the brands we reach for
        because we trust the hardware and stand behind it after a project
        wraps.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card">
        <h3>Ubiquiti</h3>
        <p>
          Modern renovations need modern networks - WiFi that actually
          reaches every room, wired drops where they're needed, and a
          system built to be expanded later. We spec Ubiquiti's UniFi
          hardware for our <a href="/services/">low-voltage and networking</a> work because
          it's professional-grade equipment that doesn't lock you into a
          subscription to keep working.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>Lutron</h3>
        <p>
          Beyond our Caseta and RadioRA 3 certifications, Lutron is simply
          the brand we reach for on lighting and shade control at every
          scale. Reliable hardware and a design language that scales from a
          single dimmer to a whole-home system.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>Elco Lighting</h3>
        <p>
          For the fixtures themselves - recessed lighting, downlights, and
          the architectural details that make a lighting design feel
          finished - we favor Elco. Well-made fixtures paired with a
          well-designed system are what separate a lighting job that just
          works from one that elevates a room.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="container">
    <div class="notice">
      <p>Curious how these fit into your renovation? Let's talk through what makes sense for your home.</p>
      <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/contact/">Get a Quote</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
